-- Test Description
-- This tests the receive functionality in gigabit mode for accepting frames 
-- much greater than allowed.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage  																																																																											  tion.
-- � Ensures that the GEM will only accept a frame up to the maximum size 
--   of 1518 bytes in 1G mode operation.
-- � Ensures that the GEM stops writing received data once the too long 
--   condition is recognised.
-- � Ensures that the GEM waits until the end of frame before reporting correct
--   status for the frame.
-- � Ensures that the GEM can accept new incoming frames immediately after an
--   excessive length frame
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
-- 1. Set wait states suitable for gigabit DMA operation
-- 2. Configure the GEM for gigabit operation using GMII and DMA interfaces.
-- 3. Ensure that the GEM is configured to accept 1518 bytes maximum.
--
-- Gigabit GMII
-- 4. Receive a 1555 byte frame (too long) with good CRC.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped and an excessive length statistic is
--    reported.
-- 5. Receive a 1555 byte frame (too long) with bad CRC.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped and an jabber statistic is reported.
-- 6. After a minimum IFG, receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC.
--    Ensure that a frame received interrupt is generated and good status
--    reported.
-- 7. Check the statistics registers to ensure that the above operation was
--    handled correctly
-- 
-- Gigabit TBI
-- 8. Enable the TBI interface mode of the GEM
-- 9. Receive a 1555 byte frame (too long) with good CRC.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped and an excessive length statistic is
--    reported.
--10. Receive a 1555 byte frame (too long) with a symbol error.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped and both jabber and symbol error
--    statistics are reported.
--11. After a minimum IFG, receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC.
--    Ensure that a frame received interrupt is generated and good status
--    reported.
--12. Check the statistics registers to ensure that the above operation was
--    handled correctly
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


